From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: compact PIN pad and Lock screen size

On a window under 560 dp tall (the Q25's 411 dp square screen) the PIN
bouncer's 72 dp round keys do not fit under the message and above the
emergency button. KeyguardPINView now gives the pad wide, short keys
(44 dp high at the Default size, up to 2.2 times as wide), a 40 dp PIN
row, 6 dp gaps and 6 dp emergency button margins, on both the legacy
ConstraintLayout pad and the MotionLayout pad that the released
lockscreen.enable_landscape flag uses (each ConstraintSet is updated).

Settings > Display > Lock screen size (Settings.Secure
sable_lock_screen_size: 0 Small, 1 Default, 2 Large, 3 Larger) scales
the keys and digits, read each time the bouncer appears; keys stop
growing where the window is full. The locked glance's text and peek
icons scale with it too. Sizes in keyguard/sable/SableLockSize (pure).

The software keyboard fallback line (0307) was only in the legacy
layouts; the motion layouts now carry it under the bouncer message.
Taller windows keep Android's pad. No authentication code changes.
